# Privacy Policy for Dupi - YT Music Playlist Organizer

**Last updated:** August 5, 2026

Dupi - YT Music Playlist Organizer ("the Extension") is an open-source browser extension committed to protecting your privacy.

## Data Collection
The Extension **does not collect, store, transmit, sell, or share any user data**.
All processing is performed **locally within your browser**. The Extension temporarily reads content from **YouTube Music (music.youtube.com)** only to provide its features, such as playlist organization, tagging, searching, duplicate detection, and sorting. This information is **never transmitted** to the developer or any third party.

## Third-Party Services
The Extension uses the public **Last.fm API** only to retrieve music metadata (such as genres and tags). Requests contain only the information necessary to identify the track being looked up. No personal information or browsing history is transmitted.

## Local Storage
User preferences, tags, playlists, exports, and other extension data are stored **locally using your browser's storage** and never leave your device.

## Analytics
The Extension does **not** use analytics, telemetry, advertising, tracking technologies, or crash reporting services.

## Contact
If you have any questions or concerns, please open an issue on the project's GitHub repository.
